/-! The repair key routine for the compact-control instance in the radices
`2^q`, `2^b`, on seventeen tapes: split the rank from the counter into the two
address words, run the guard test and write the membership flag at the key's
origin, run the inverse packed program and the ideal toggle, append the
destination words to the key when flagged, and erase every scratch word.
The counter, control and constants are preserved; the key holds the flag
word of the repair scan; the cost is linear in the address width. -/

namespace IntegerMultBounds.Machine.KeyRoutine

open ColumnTransducer (Rule)

/-- The seventeen-tape bank: key, counter, `V`, `W`, control, three
constants, four inverse-program words, offset scratch, recovered `V`, order
cell, flag word, toggled `V`. -/
def bank (f0 f1 f2 f3 f4 f5 f6 f7 f8 f9 f10 f11 f12 f13 f14 f15 f16 : ℤ → Fin 5)
    (p0 p1 p2 p3 p4 p5 p6 p7 p8 p9 p10 p11 p12 p13 p14 p15 p16 : ℤ) : Tapes 17 1 :=
  ⟨fun i => if i = 0 then p0 else if i = 1 then p1 else if i = 2 then p2 else if i = 3 then p3
    else if i = 4 then p4 else if i = 5 then p5 else if i = 6 then p6 else if i = 7 then p7
    else if i = 8 then p8 else if i = 9 then p9 else if i = 10 then p10 else if i = 11 then p11
    else if i = 12 then p12 else if i = 13 then p13 else if i = 14 then p14 else if i = 15 then p15
    else p16,
   fun i => if i = 0 then f0 else if i = 1 then f1 else if i = 2 then f2 else if i = 3 then f3
    else if i = 4 then f4 else if i = 5 then f5 else if i = 6 then f6 else if i = 7 then f7
    else if i = 8 then f8 else if i = 9 then f9 else if i = 10 then f10 else if i = 11 then f11
    else if i = 12 then f12 else if i = 13 then f13 else if i = 14 then f14 else if i = 15 then f15
    else f16⟩

